Package: MultiOmicQC
Title: Quality control for Multi-omics datasets
Version: 0.0.16
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcel", "Ramos", email = "marcel.ramos@sph.cuny.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("MultiAssay", "SIG", email = "biocmultiassay@googlegroups.com",
    role = "ctb"))
Description: This package provides functions for quality control of
    multi-omics datasets represented as MultiAssayExperiment objects.
    It checks the compatibility of genomic annotations, such as seqlevels,
    seqlengths, seqlevelsStyle, and genome builds, across ranged
    experiments and provides helpers for harmonizing them. Sample-level
    helpers, such as clustering on marker features, support checks of
    sample identity against clinical annotations.
Depends: R (>= 4.6.0),
    MultiAssayExperiment
Imports:
    BiocBaseUtils,
    GenomeInfoDb,
    methods,
    Seqinfo,
    stats,
    S4Vectors,
    SummarizedExperiment,
    utils
Suggests:
